#. Tag: title
#: plugins-chapter.docbook:3
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plugins"
msgstr "Ajustons"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins-chapter.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&korganizer; provides you the possibility of extending the application with "
"plugins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins-chapter.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The plugins can be configured under the &korganizer; main configuration "
"dialog Choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem> Configure "
"&korganizer;</guimenuitem></menuchoice> or <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem> Configure Calendar</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, inside "
"&kontact;, and click the <guilabel>Plugin</guilabel> icon on the icon list "
"sidebar of the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins-chapter.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid "Available Plugins"
msgstr "Ajustons disponibles"

#. Tag: title
#: plugins-chapter.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "Date Numbers Plugin for Calendars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins-chapter.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This plugin adds the day number of day in the the year to the agenda view. "
"For instance, February 1 is the day number 32."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins-chapter.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "Jewish Calendar Plugin"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins-chapter.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The plugin provides you a the the Jewish calendar dates in addition to the "
"Gregorian calendar dates. In the configuration dialog of the plugin, you can "
"choose if you want to display Israeli holidays, weekly prasha, day of Omer "
"and / or Chol HaMoed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins-chapter.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid "Journal Print Style"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins-chapter.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid "The plugin allows you to print journal (diary) entries."
msgstr ""
